META GLASSES PAIRING AND CAPTURE PROTOCOL (2026-09-19)

- The Android `Pair Meta glasses` action opens Meta AI (`com.facebook.stella`) so the
  presenter can show the real companion-app handoff. Returning to MemoryPalace completes a
  clearly labelled simulated connection because the team does not have physical glasses.
- The current working recorder is still the rear phone camera. Its protocol is authenticated
  JSON over HTTP: `GET /commands` supplies short-lived `start`/`stop` actions,
  `POST /commands/ack` confirms them with the recording ID, and `/media` receives the MP4.
- For real glasses, the official protocol is Meta Wearables Device Access Toolkit v0.9:
  `Wearables.startRegistration(activity)` deep-links to Meta AI, the app requests
  `Permission.CAMERA`, creates a `DeviceSession`, adds the camera capability, and calls
  `stream.start()` to collect frames. The application would encode those frames for the same
  10-second moment pipeline. It is not represented as a REST “record glasses” endpoint.
- The SDK is still developer preview and needs a Wearables Developer Center project,
  callback scheme, supported glasses/firmware, Bluetooth permissions, and user consent.

